$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 3-(4-fluorophenyl)propiolonitrile (2f) [CAS 575433-43-1] A flame-dried
20-mL Schlenk tube equipped with a J. Young valve was charged with
CuOTf·toluene (20.7 mg, 40 μmol), ICN (152.9 mg, 1.0 mmol), and THF (1.6
mL) under nitrogen atmosphere. (4-Fluorophenyl)acetylene (1f; 48.1 mg,
0.40 mmol) and 2,2,6,6-tetramethylpiperidine (101.3 μL, 0.60 mmol) was
added to the solution, and the resulting mixture was stirred at 60°C for
17 h. The reaction was quenched by adding sat. NaHCO3 aq. The aqueous
layer was extracted with 4 mL of AcOEt for three times. The combined
organic extract was washed with sat. Na2S2O3 aq, dried over MgSO4,
filtered, and concentrated under vacuum. The residue was subjected to
column chromatography on silica gel (hexane/EtOAc = 40/1) to give alkynyl
cyanide 2f as a pale yellow solid (38.5 mg, 0.27 mmol, 66%). Mp
64.5-65.0°C. IR (nujol): 2279, 1601, 1508 cm-1. 1H NMR (CDCl3): δ 6.90
(d, J =8.8 Hz, 2H), 7.56 (d, J = 8.8 Hz, 2H). 13C NMR (CDCl3): δ 63.1,
81.9, 105.3, 113.7 (d, J = 3.3 Hz), 116.6 (d, J = 22.3 Hz), 135.9 (d, J =
9.1 Hz), 164.6 (d, J = 256.2 Hz).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
