$DATUM Cyclization Add cyanogen bromide (7.88 g, 0.074 mol) to a solution of
4-phenylethynyl-N2-(1-(R)-methyl-2,2-dimethylpropyl)benzene-1,2-diamine
in absolute ethanol (500 mL) and stir 4.5h. Concentrate and redissolve in
dichloromethane, wash with saturated sodium bicarbonate and purify
(silica gel chromatography with dichloromethane/methanol mixtures to give
16.9 g (quant) of the title compound as a tan solid.
6-Phenylethynyl-1-(1-(R)-methyl-2,2-dimethylpropyl)-1H-benzimidazol-2-ylamine;
yield 16.9 g (quant). MS (ES+H): m/z = 318.2.
