$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Method 1: Amide-coupling. The
concerned carboxylic acid and N,N-diisopropylethylamine (1.05 eq.) are
added into dichloromethane and stirred at RT for 15 minutes. A solution
of the aniline derivative (1.0 eq.) in dichloromethane is subsequently
added dropwise. O-(benzotriazol-1-yl)-N,N,N',N'-tetramethyluronium
tetrafluoroborate (1.05 eq.) is added, and the mixture is stirred
overnight at room temperature. The reaction solution is subsequently
washed with water, with saturated aqueous sodium hydrogen carbonate
solution and again with water. The solvent is removed in vacuum, and the
residue is mixed with ethyl acetate. The precipitated solid is filtered
and washed with pentane. The filtrate is concentrated in vacuum and the
residue is purified by column chromatography.
N-{4-[(2-{[tert-Butyl(dimethyl)silyl]oxy}ethyl)amino]phenyl}-N'-(4-ethynyl-phenyl)pyrazine-2,3-dicarboxamide.
According to the General Method 1, 400 mg (1.50 mmol) of the compound
from Example 7A and 398 mg (1.50 mmol) of the compound from Example 1A
are reacted. Yield: 376 mg (49% of theory). LC-MS (Method 2): Rt = 3.08
min; MS (ESIpos): m/z= 516[M+H]+.
