$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):SOL(4):CAS_RN
$DATUM 67-66-3
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Step 4: To a solution of the sulfinamide from
step 3 (3.80 g, 7.6 mmol) in CH2Cl2/MeOH (3:1 80 mL) was added a solution
of 4 M HCl (dioxane) (11.4 mL, 45.4 mmol). The resultant solution was
stirred at RT for 1.5 hours. The solution was concentrated. The residue
was re-concentrated from toluene (lx). The residue was then taken up in
CHCl3 and TFA (26 mL, 1 : 1). To this solution was added
1,3-dimethoxybenzene (6.5 mL, 50 mmol). The resultant solution was
stirred at RT overnight. The resultant solution was concentrated. The
resultant oil was partitioned between Et2O and 1 M HCl (aq.). The aqueous
layer was extracted with Et2O (2x). The aqueous layer was then adjusted
to pH 10 with the addition of sat. Na2CO3 (aq.). The aqueous layer was
extracted with CH2Cl2 (3x). The organic layers were extracted from the
basic aqueous layer, combined, dried over Na2SO4, filtered and
concentrated.
