$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Step 1: To a solution of
2,4-difloroacetophenone (15,0 g, 96 mmol) in THF (100 mL) was added
(R)-2-methyl-2-propanesulfinamide (12.8 g, 106 mmol) and Ti(OEt)4, (32.0
g, 120 mmol). The resultant solution was heated to reflux overnight.
After that time, the solution was cooled to RT and poured onto ice. To
this mixture was added CH2Cl2 and the resultant mixture was stirred at RT
for 10 min. The mixture was then filtered through Celite. The filter cake
was washed with CH2Cl2. The layers were separated. The aqueous layer was
extracted with CH2Cl2 (2x), The combined organic layers were dried over
Na2SO4, filtered and concentrated. The crude product was purified via
flash chromatography (SiO2: gradient elution 100:0 to 45:55
hexanes:EtOAc).
