$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):SOL(1):CAS_RN
$DATUM 127-19-5
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Step 1: CuI (7.6 mg, 0.04 mmol) was added to a solution of iodoaniline
(200 mg, 0.39 mmol, Scheme 10a), diisopropylamine (0.169 mL, 1.2 mmol),
PdCl2(PPh3)2 (28 mg, 0.04 mmol) and phenyl acetylene (0.132 mL, 1.2 mmol)
in dimethylacetamide (2 mL), and the reaction was stirred at 40°C for 6
h. The reaction was diluted with sat. aqueous NaHCO3 solution and EtOAc,
then filtered reaction over celite. After rinsing the residue with EtOAc,
the aqueous layer was extracted with EtOAc (3 x). The combined organic
layers were dried over Na2SO4, filtered, and concentrated to give a
residue that was subsequently subjected to silica gel chromatography
(10→20 % EtOAc/hexanes). The anilino acetylene intermediate (181 mg,
95%).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
